    <string name="app_name">SubRead Anki</string>
    <string name="add_label">Add to Anki</string>
    <string name="capture_label">SubRead Anki: the sentence and a screenshot for a card</string>
    <string name="capture_summary">Keeps the last text selection and a screenshot for the card.</string>
    <string name="capture_description">SubRead Anki uses this service for one thing: when you select a text in an app, it keeps that text and takes a screenshot, so that the next card gets the sentence around the word and a picture of the screen. It reads nothing else, keeps only the last selection and the last screenshot, and sends nothing anywhere.</string>

    <string name="about">One tap makes an Anki card: the word, its reading and definition, the sentence it is in, a screenshot, the word audio and the sentence audio. Select a word in any app and choose "Add to Anki" in the menu, share a text, or tap the Anki button in SubRead Dictionary or SubRead Overlay.</string>
    <string name="privacy">The card goes to AnkiDroid on this device. Nothing leaves the device.</string>

